[size=4][b][color=#D8B45D]INSTALLATION[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the current [b]Windows Portable[/b] file from the Files tab or official Releases page.
[*]Place it in a normal writable folder. It does not need to live inside the game directory.
[*]Run Dragonwilds Sync and complete Guided Setup.
[*]Confirm the detected retail game and/or dedicated-server directory.
[*]Create, adopt, import, or connect to a World profile.
[*]Review the manifest and synchronization receipt before launching.
[/list]

Updates are published through the application's GitHub-backed update channel. Dedicated hosts can also create Quick or Headless desktop shortcuts for a selected profile.

[spoiler=IMPORTANT SAFETY AND PLATFORM NOTES]
[list]
[*]Back up irreplaceable Worlds before adopting or modifying them. Dragonwilds Sync uses backup-first workflows, but an external save backup is still wise.
[*]Router forwarding, carrier-grade NAT, third-party firewalls, VPN behavior, and WAN reachability depend on the host's real environment.
[*]Ubuntu AppImage and Linux/Proton support have automated build paths, but real game/runtime combinations remain hardware and distribution dependent.
[*]Antivirus products may inspect a portable executable that launches a bundled local service. Do not disable protection globally. Use an official release, review the source, and verify its published hash when in doubt.
[*]Dragonwilds Sync never needs a personal Nexus API key bundled into the application.
[/list]
[/spoiler]

